{title: 116 - Of the Father's Love Begotten}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #116 • DIVNUM MYSTERIUM   (13TH CENTURY PLAINSONG, MODE V) • 8.7.8.7.8.7.9}
{lyricist: J. M. Neale and H. W. Baker}
{composer: 13th century plainsong}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 116}
{meta: tune DIVNUM MYSTERIUM   (13TH CENTURY PLAINSONG, MODE V)}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7.8.7.9}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm]Of the Father's [Bb]love [Cm/G]begotten,
[Bb7]Ere the worlds [Eb]began [Bb7/Ab]to be,
[Cm]He is [Bb]Alpha [Bb7/Ab]and Omega,
[Cm/G]He [Ab]the [Bb]source, [Cm/G]the [Gm]ending [Bb7]He,
[Eb]Of the things that are, that have [Bb/F]been,
[Gm]And that [Eb/Bb]future [Ab]years shall [Gm/D]see,
[Eb]Evermore and [Cm]evermore! [Bb]Amen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]O ye heights [Bb]of heaven [Cm/G]adore [Bb7/Ab]Him;
[Bb7]Angel hosts, [Eb]His [Fm]praises [Bb7]sing;
[Cm]Powers, dominions, [Bb7/Ab]bow before Him,
[Cm/G]And [Ab]extol [Cm/G]our [Gm]God [Bb7/Ab]and King;
[Eb]Let no tongue on earth be silent,
[Gm]Every [Eb/Bb]voice in [Ab]concert [Gm/D]ring,
[Eb]Evermore and [Cm]evermore! [Bb]Amen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]Christ, to Thee [Bb]with God [Cm/G]the [Bb7/Ab]Father
[Bb7]And, O Holy [Fm]Ghost, [Bb7/Ab]to Thee,
[Cm]Hymn and [Bb]chant and [Bb7/Ab]high thanksgiving
[Cm/G]And [Ab]unwearied [Gm]praises [Bb7/Ab]be.
[Eb]Honor, glory, and dominion,
[Gm]And eternal [Ab]victory,
[Eb]Evermore and [Cm]evermore! [Bb]Amen.
{end_of_verse}
